Short:    HD-Installer for Formula One Grand Prix V2.0b
Author:   Codetapper/Action (codetapper@hotmail.com), ICQ: 26051687
Uploader: Codetapper/Action (codetapper@hotmail.com)
Version:  2.0b
Type:     game/patch

This patch applies to "Formula One Grand Prix" (c) 1991 Microprose.
Supported: - 4 disk original release/PowerPlus budget release (Mad-Matt)
           - 3 disk release (A600 Wild, Weird & Wicked pack) (Mad-Matt)

REQUIREMENTS:
- Slave requires WHDLoad V20+ and an installed A500 Kickstart 1.3 image
- Game requires 512k chip mem and 768k other memory (+3.2Mb other memory 
  for preload option). MEMCONFIG=1, set in the supplied icons, raises
  this to 932k other memory. Remove the MEMCONFIG tooltype on machines
  without fast memory

FEATURES:
- Full load from HD
- Manual protection removed (type anything at the prompt)
- Fully compatible with F1GP-Ed modifications to the game file!
- Intro can be skipped by pressing fire/left mouse while loading or by
  setting the CUSTOM1=1 tooltype
- Full 1991 season drivers and teams replace the built-in names unless you
  have modified your version of the game with F1GP-Ed (2.0b: unless any
  driver, team or engine name was changed)
- All save operations default to a "saves" subdirectory so as not to
  clutter up the main game directory
- Filter button enabled by default when loading/saving (prevents the list
  of files showing invalid files)
- Audio filter disabled for clearer sound
- Mouse pointer sped up to maximum speed
- Normal, RomIcon, NewIcons and OS3.5+ Colour Icons (created by Frank,
  Mad-Matt and myself) and 2 Exoticons from http://exotica.fix.no/
- Quit option (default key is 'F10')

HISTORY:

Version 2.0b (31.10.2026) by Vesuri (beta):
- Consistent game speed on a 68020 or better: the race runs in real time
  however long the 3D view takes to draw. A 68000 keeps the original timing
- Smooth motion on a 68020 or better: the 3D view is drawn between the
  game's updates, up to every frame on fast Amigas
- Faster 3D drawing on a 68020 or better with fast memory (MEMCONFIG=1)
- Slightly faster 3D drawing on a 68000
- Optional CPU caches
- All of the above are enabled in the supplied icons (CUSTOM2=1531
  MEMCONFIG=1). Uncheck them in the WHDLoad startup options to play the
  original game. Leave the other developer options unchecked
- The enhancements apply to the 4 disk release's game file only, and
  only while the game code they change is the original. F1GP-Ed's settings
  keep it; a game file changed there by other means runs without them
- F1GP-Ed's cockpit designs and replaced backdrops work with the
  enhancements; the gear indicator is drawn where the cockpit puts it
- F1GP-Ed's frame rate setting (used by its 1995-2002 datafiles) sets how
  often the game updates the world; the race runs in real time at that
  rate, and motion stays smooth between the updates
- "Developer - 20 Hz world step" (off in the supplied icons) updates the
  world 20 times a second instead of 8, or instead of an F1GP-Ed file's
  rate, as F1GP-Ed's 20 fps setting does. Replays and saved games only
  work at the rate they were made with
- The computer cars lose speed in corners at every world update, so a
  finer step slows them (8-9% a lap at 20 Hz, as F1GP-Ed's guide warns).
  With the 20 Hz step the slave makes the loss the same each second as
  at the original rate, and their laps are within 2% of the original's;
  "Developer - native AI cornering loss at 20 Hz" keeps the original
  loss. "Developer - AI cornering loss a second (file's rate)" does the
  same at an F1GP-Ed file's own frame rate, where the effect is small
  (under 1% a lap at the 1995-2002 datafiles' rate). F1GP-Ed's suggested
  speed factor correction for 20 fps is no longer needed with it
- Fixed: at finer world steps (20 Hz, or F1GP-Ed's 25 fps) a car carrying
  a lot of fuel spun by itself, as F1GP-Ed's guide warns for long races.
  Always on; the original rate is unaffected
- "Developer - local speed factors" (off in the supplied icons) gives the
  computer cars the per-circuit Local Speed Factors of an F1GP-Ed datafile
  saved as F1GP-Ed.f1gp in the data directory, as F1GP-Ed's memory patch
  does, in place of the game file's Speed Factor. The wet weather reduction
  and risk factors are not applied
- Requires WHDLoad V20+

Version 1.0 (06.12.2002) by Codetapper/Action:
- Initial release

I recommend anyone that enjoys this game to download the superb F1GP-Ed
from Aminet (game/misc/F1GP-Ed.lha) or from Oliver's Amiga F1 website at
http://www.nanunanu.org/~oliver/AmigaF1.html

Using F1GP-Ed you can modify an enormous number of parameters associated
with the game and this WHDLoad patch will still work correctly! If you
wish to modify the game regularly, I recommend you to add an assign to
your s:user-startup file like so:

  assign f1gp_disk_#2: games:FormulaOneGrandPrix/data

Replace the path with wherever you installed the game. If you do this,
when you launch F1GP-Ed it will find the game file straight away.

The install script will automatically create a "saves" directory which is
the default directory for any information which is loaded or saved.  If you
really want to save information in the main directory, press the "DH0:"
button to access it.

The kickstart image must be located in the directory "Devs:Kickstarts"
and must be named "kick34005.A500". The image can be extracted from an
A500 with tools like "GrabKick" or similar which can be found on Aminet.
If the image is the wrong version or altered in any way, WHDLoad will
quit with an appropriate error message. 

Additionally the file "kick34005.A500.RTB" must be installed in the same
directory as the kickstart image. It can be found in the archive 
"util/boot/skick343.lha" on Aminet.

Greetings to Mad-Matt for the original quick install, supplying both
originals, testing and the great front and back box scan icon, Frank for
his awesome icons, Wepl for WHDLoad, all Action members, my testing crew
and the WHDLoad team!


Codetapper/Action (06-Dec-2002)


